{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786772520096744001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"reclinable-ammonitic-hound","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"7339d9117791003dd9f2aab830e360799b62e736d198e4e7604a3bcb8135ac72","event_uuid":"689020bc-e3c4-472b-9344-e61156c7c7ef","position":{"commit_sha":"dc3cefbe2063d1f7b65c333aede4d162dd85bed1","position":"1786764663406395001-689020bc-e3c4-472b-9344-e61156c7c7ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"59bb7e71ec228064a7b34068b19a5d5897781688ab9681b60182567ee2862062","event_uuid":"223ca9a7-4f91-4677-876a-ec8cc04b1e16","position":{"commit_sha":"ff643d6c88d7bc4fa526df59601ce5a9c1ef5358","position":"1786764679254818001-223ca9a7-4f91-4677-876a-ec8cc04b1e16"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786764663406395001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"# Land dependabot PR #127 (uv-lock group) through Gerrit — pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2 only; mcp 2.0 stays deferred to 732b\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror for this project: dependabot keeps opening dependency PRs\nthere, but they can never merge — the content has to be re-applied locally and landed as a\nGerrit change, then the PR closed by hand. PR #127 (\"deps: bump the uv-lock group across 1\ndirectory with 3 updates\", branch `dependabot/uv/uv-lock-dd93acce05`) proposes three bumps:\n\n* `pypandoc-binary` `1.15` -> `1.17` — pinned EXACTLY in the `wiki` extra and the `dev`\n  group (the exact pin is deliberate: byte-safety tests assert byte-level pandoc output, so\n  local and CI must ship the identical binary).\n* `ruff` `0.16.1` -> `0.16.2` — pinned EXACTLY in the `dev` group (pre-commit hook, local\n  `make lint`, and CI must run the identical ruff).\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (major), with the pyproject ceiling loosened `<2` -> `<3` in\n  both the `mcp` and `dev` extras.\n\nThe `mcp` half is the THIRD re-proposal of the same major bump (PRs #124, #125, now #127).\nIt was investigated under ticket 1dfd (entodermic-dizzying-pikeperch) and rejected on\nevidence: mcp 2.0 removes the `mcp.server.fastmcp` module (verified `ModuleNotFoundError`)\nthat `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` import; the structural\nmigration (FastMCP -> MCPServer, transport params moved off the constructor, mcp-types\nsplit, sse-starlette >=3, lifespan/worker-thread/421 behavioral audits) is already tracked\nas its own open epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b` (bared-nickel-insect), \"Migrate MCP server to\nmcp 2.0 (fastmcp removal)\", whose migrate-vs-defer analysis explicitly recommends staying\non `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` until 2.0.x has patch releases. PR #125 applied the same path-2\ndecision rule (ticket carnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso, Gerrit change 1483). Re-litigating\nit here would duplicate 732b, so this ticket lands only the safe subset.\n\n## Approach\n\nLand the **safe subset** of PR #127 — the `pypandoc-binary` and `ruff` bumps — and leave\nthe `mcp` ceiling at `<2` so the resolver keeps `mcp` 1.29.0, consistent with tickets 1dfd\nand carnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso.\n\nConcretely, in a fresh worktree (`../deps-bump`) branched from current `origin/main`:\n\n1. Edit `pyproject.toml`: `\"pypandoc-binary==1.15\"` -> `\"pypandoc-binary==1.17\"` in BOTH\n   the `wiki` extra and the `dev` group (the notice test enforces a single distinct pin\n   value); `\"ruff==0.16.1\"` -> `\"ruff==0.16.2\"` in the `dev` group. Keep both pins exact.\n2. Refresh the lock with `uv lock --upgrade-package pypandoc-binary --upgrade-package ruff`\n   so `uv.lock` is regenerated by uv rather than hand-edited (CI gates on\n   `uv lock --check`). Then `uv sync` the dev environment so the new wheels are installed.\n3. **pandoc provenance**: pypandoc-binary bumps typically change the BUNDLED pandoc\n   executable. Determine the new bundled version empirically\n   (`python -c \"import pypandoc; print(pypandoc.get_pandoc_version())\"`). If it differs\n   from 3.6.1, update `NOTICE` (the `Version:` line and the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel\n   reference) and the version-string assertion in\n   `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` (the `\"3.6.1\" in text` line) so the GPL\n   provenance record matches what actually ships. Do NOT touch the upstream-URL assertion\n   (`\"pandoc.org\" in text or ...`) — a parallel change owns that exact line and the two\n   diffs must rebase cleanly past each other.\n4. **ruff verdict drift**: ruff changes lint/format rules between releases. Run\n   `make lint`; if 0.16.2 flags existing code or reformats files, apply the minimal fix\n   and note it in the commit message. NEVER touch `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n5. Do NOT touch the `mcp` constraints, `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 —\n   those are 732b's edit-set.\n6. Verify (`make lint && make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit`, and the wiki-renderer\n   byte-safety/pandoc tests since the bundled binary changed), commit with a\n   `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off, push `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, and\n   leave the ticket `in_progress` while the orchestrator shepherds `LLM-Review` and\n   `Verified`; the ticket closes only after the change merges and PR #127 is closed with a\n   provenance comment pointing the mcp half at 732b.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `pyproject.toml` — the two `pypandoc-binary==` pins (`wiki` extra + `dev` group) and the\n  single `ruff==` pin in the `dev` group.\n* `uv.lock` — the regenerated `pypandoc-binary` and `ruff` entries plus whatever\n  incidental churn `uv lock` emits.\n* `NOTICE` + `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` — only if the bundled pandoc\n  version changed (expected), and never the upstream-URL assertion line.\n* Minimal source fixes ONLY if ruff 0.16.2 changes a lint/format verdict on existing code.\n* OUT: the `mcp` 1.29.0 -> 2.0.0 bump and its `<2` -> `<3` ceiling move (deferred to epic\n  `732b-51df-acf2-477b` / bared-nickel-insect — already filed, so no new ticket is needed);\n  `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; ADR 0050; `.github/complexity-baseline.json`;\n  dependabot configuration; any other open dependency PR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `pyproject.toml` contains `pypandoc-binary==1.17` (twice: `wiki` + `dev`) and\n  `ruff==0.16.2`, and still contains `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` in both the `mcp` extra and the\n  `dev` group — checked with `grep -nE 'pypandoc-binary==|ruff==|mcp>=' pyproject.toml`.\n- [ ] AC2: `uv.lock` records `pypandoc-binary` at `1.17`, `ruff` at `0.16.2`, and `mcp`\n  at `1.29.0` — checked with `grep -A1 -E '^name = \"(pypandoc-binary|ruff|mcp)\"$' uv.lock`\n  — and `uv lock --check` exits 0 (the same gate CI runs).\n- [ ] AC3: `NOTICE` names the pandoc version actually bundled by pypandoc-binary 1.17\n  (verified empirically via `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` in the synced worktree venv)\n  and references `pypandoc-binary==1.17`; `pytest tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py`\n  exits 0.\n- [ ] AC4: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` exits 0 in the worktree under\n  ruff 0.16.2, `make typecheck` exits 0, and `pytest tests/unit` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC5: A Gerrit change carrying this diff exists on refs/for/main with this ticket's\n  `rebar-ticket:` trailer and a DCO sign-off — checked with `git log -1 --format=%B HEAD`\n  and the Gerrit change URL printed by the push.\n- [ ] AC6: The mcp 2.0 half is NOT landed: no edit to the `mcp` constraints, and the\n  deferral is recorded as a comment on this ticket naming epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b` —\n  checked by `git diff origin/main --stat` showing no `_optionality.yml`/ADR-0050 change\n  and `rebar show <this>` showing the comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"bump pypandoc-binary==1.15 -> 1.17 (wiki extra + dev group) and ruff==0.16.1 -> 0.16.2 (dev group); mcp ceiling stays <2"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"regenerated by uv lock --upgrade-package for pypandoc-binary and ruff; mcp stays 1.29.0"},{"path":"NOTICE","reason":"update bundled pandoc version and pypandoc-binary wheel reference if the bundled pandoc changed (expected)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py","reason":"update the bundled-pandoc version-string assertion only; upstream-URL assertion line untouched (owned by a parallel change)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"dc89-cd11-acd6-4e61","ticket_type":"task","title":"Land dependabot PR #127 through Gerrit: pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2 (mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["689020bc-e3c4-472b-9344-e61156c7c7ef","223ca9a7-4f91-4677-876a-ec8cc04b1e16"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786772520096744001,"uuid":"1e53158d-9cc3-4933-a6eb-04fa5f7b0987"}